WEBVTT

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:16.490
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:33.920
Wolf's Occupation Change.

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:40.250
Oh, so busy, so busy!

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:42.160
If I don't hurry, 
I'm going to be late!

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:47.620
Don't suck me up!

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:47.620
Oh?

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:50.210
What was that about?

00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:55.460
Sorry. I have to leave soon, 
so I'm in a hurry.

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:57.510
I know.

00:01:57.510 --> 00:01:59.840
As an apology...

00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:04.240
So, she gave you these?

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:07.990
Seriously, I don't know what 
I'm going to do with my mom.

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:12.270
Vacuums should just disappear 
from the world.

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:15.240
I don't think they need to disappear.

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:19.360
The way vacuums are used at 
your house is rather unique.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:24.130
Thank you for the food.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:28.540
Hey, this is good.

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:32.050
Are those sweets from Toraya, Panda?

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:35.320
I don't know. Ask my mom.

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:39.020
It's the perfect form for 
a fish-lover like me

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:40.470
and it tastes great, too.

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:42.510
Sweets from Toraya are great.

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:43.710
Oh.

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:45.590
Mr. Penguin.

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:47.610
Would you like to try our sweets, too?

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:48.600
You have some?

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.150
Sure, I'll have some.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:53.520
Here you go.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:56.270
It's a coelacanth.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:58.470
It's made very well,

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:02.490
but I'm not sure about sweets
shaped like a living fossil.

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:05.660
Were you offended?

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:07.600
Just a bit.

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:14.150
Toraya

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:13.710
What?! You're quitting as of today?

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:17.840
Damn, that Zebra...

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:22.170
Those herbivores have no guts.

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:26.920
Hello.

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:30.000
Oh, hey, Wolf.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.670
What brings you here so early?

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:33.390
Are you off today?

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:35.980
Yeah, actually...

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:39.190
I quit the bakery last month.

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:41.710
Why?!

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:46.150
The work hours were too 
long and I hurt my back.

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:48.870
Whoa, are you all right?

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:53.080
It would seem that I'm not 
fit to work at a bakery.

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:56.320
What? You're beating yourself up again?

00:03:57.060 --> 00:04:00.050
You don't have time to sit around being depressed.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:02.130
You're a carnivore!

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:03.510
Show some guts and go at it!

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:07.060
But I'm not as strong 
as you are, Tiger!

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:08.470
Neither physically or mentally!

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:11.930
You're a fierce beast! 
Don't talk so meekly!

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:14.970
Stop calling me a "fierce beast."

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:18.130
I'm nothing but an overgrown mutt.

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:19.500
Hey...

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:21.400
You're a fierce beast, too...

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:23.360
I'm...

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:34.190
Japan Cross Country Tour!!

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:27.120
...going to forget about the bakery

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:29.310
and just ride across Japan on a bicycle.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:30.420
Hey...

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:34.210
simply riding across Japan doesn't 
mean you'll find yourself.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:36.170
Then...

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:39.850
I'll write poems and sell them 
in front of the station.

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:44.130
Well, I'm a Wolf 
- by Wolf

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:43.590
Well, yeah, you are a wolf, but...

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:46.090
Oh, I know...

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:50.980
How about you help me with the shop?

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:52.060
What?

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:55.020
One of my part-timers 
just quit, so I'm in a bind.

00:04:55.610 --> 00:04:57.100
So, how about it?

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:00.040
S-Sure.

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:03.860
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:11.290
So you're having some more today, Mr. Penguin?

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:15.000
Japanese

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:15.000
I'm in the mood for Japanese sweets 
instead of raw fish today.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:16.460
Mr. Penguin.

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:19.990
I have a bad feeling about this...

00:05:19.990 --> 00:05:21.550
You made something, didn't you?

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:23.260
Was it obvious?

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:27.470
All right. I'll give it a gander.

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:29.930
This would be it.

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:32.260
It's a ranchu.

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:34.490
Would you put it away?

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:38.940
Toraya

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:46.360
Hello.

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:49.070
Welcome!

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:52.280
Oh, well if it isn't Mr. Wolf.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:57.020
Didn't you used to work 
at Monkey's Bakery?

00:05:57.020 --> 00:05:59.020
Actually, don't work there anymore.

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:00.600
I hurt my back.

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:01.720
Oh my.

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:03.030
Are you all right?

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:04.830
Um, yes...

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:08.380
I'm working here part-time 
until I find another job.

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:09.660
Oh my.

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:12.160
I hope you feel better soon.

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:14.460
Yes. Thank you very much.

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:18.390
So, what would you like today?

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:19.520
Oh.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:22.180
I'd like five of these 
porcupine buns.

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:22.820
Right away.

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:28.170
I'm going to visit a friend today, 
and she's a Yama Arashi fan.

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:30.280
Oh, I see.

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:34.000
Even though we're small

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:35.630
Oh, but maybe it's imprudent 
to eat porcupines...

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:36.170
We're unstoppable!

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:38.300
Maybe we shouldn't eat them?

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:40.250
Drum with our feet

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:40.250
Maybe it's okay to eat them?

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:44.750
I think eating them would be fine.

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:50.930
Thank you very much.

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:55.770
Hey, you can take a break.

00:06:56.690 --> 00:06:57.890
Oh, thanks.

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:05.770
Tiger,

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:07.780
please help yourself to these.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:10.070
You gave me some of the 
shop's red bean paste

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:11.740
so I made some buns with them.

00:07:12.210 --> 00:07:13.480
Wow.

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:22.370
They're... delicious!

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:23.920
The bread is so fragrant!

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:26.400
I added wheat bran into the dough.

00:07:26.810 --> 00:07:27.720
Wheat bran?

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:30.790
It's the skin and germ of the wheat.

00:07:31.370 --> 00:07:34.640
It becomes more fragrant than 
using whole wheat flour.

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:39.100
<i>It goes really well with 
our red bean paste.</i>

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:44.100
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:49.870
You've been eating those 
every day lately.

00:07:51.850 --> 00:07:52.990
Mr. Penguin.

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:55.880
You don't have to bring 
out anything else.

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:01.500
Toraya

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:00.960
Hello.

00:08:01.950 --> 00:08:03.100
Welcome.

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:08.170
So that friend I mentioned 
visiting the other day...

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:10.710
Her husband is a baker.

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:13.430
Do you know of Donkey's Bakery?

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:15.380
O-Of course!

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:20.060
Their bread is incredibly delicious.
I really admire them.

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:21.980
They were looking for a new hire.

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:23.380
Wha?!

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:26.360
No, no. I couldn't.

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:28.690
I still have much to learn.

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:31.150
Sounds like a great opportunity to me.

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:33.610
Mr. Tiger.

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:36.480
Despite how he looks,

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:38.770
he really knows what he's doing.

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:40.740
But...

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:43.540
I knew as soon as I ate your buns.

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:46.750
If Mr. Tiger says so, 
there's no doubt about it.

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:49.310
But please wait...

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:53.740
I'm definitely not skilled enough 
to work at Mr. Donkey's...

00:08:54.270 --> 00:08:56.510
I don't think they were in any hurry.

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:58.800
I just wanted to tell 
you just in case.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:03.230
Thank you very much.

00:09:06.460 --> 00:09:07.710
Wolf.

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:09.800
What is it, Tiger?

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:12.180
Once you're done training at a bakery,

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:13.940
you were going to open 
your own place, right?

00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:18.910
I was just thinking...
it'd be nice if I could do that.

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:20.900
When that happens,

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:23.000
You can use our red bean
paste in your buns.

00:09:23.350 --> 00:09:24.460
What?!

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:27.260
But... Toraya's red bean paste...

00:09:27.260 --> 00:09:30.380
Mr. Donkey wanted desperately 
to use it at his bakery,

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:32.220
but you refused, didn't you?

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:33.960
You idiot.

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:35.920
I'd give you some because it's you.

00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:43.560
Even Lion said that when 
you open your own shop,

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:45.850
he'd invest in it and was 
looking forward to it.

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:48.930
Lion said that?

00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:51.160
Mr. Grizzly, too.

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:55.780
I'd be more than happy to have 
his baked goods at my bar.

00:09:56.440 --> 00:10:00.620
Everyone is waiting for you 
to come into your own.

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:03.500
T-Tiger...

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:08.280
All of you are supposed 
to be fierce beasts,

00:10:08.280 --> 00:10:09.750
but you're so kind.

00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:13.600
I'll do my best for everyone's sake!

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:15.050
That's more like it!

00:10:15.580 --> 00:10:17.260
Our bond...

00:10:20.810 --> 00:10:22.780
...is tighter than beef tendon.

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:29.140
Donkey's Bakery

00:10:24.630 --> 00:10:26.150
Hello, nice to meet you.

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:29.140
My name is Wolf and I came here 
on Panda Mama's referral.

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:31.050
Please, have a seat.

00:10:31.510 --> 00:10:33.140
Do you have your resume?

00:10:33.140 --> 00:10:35.110
Yes. I have it right here.

00:10:37.480 --> 00:10:39.150
Thank you for your consideration.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:44.700
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:51.150
Toraya

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:57.460
What's the matter, Tiger?

00:10:57.930 --> 00:10:59.800
You seem preoccupied.

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:02.660
I keep thinking

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:06.250
that you'll hear back
 about your interview today,

00:11:06.250 --> 00:11:07.770
so I've been on edge.

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:09.420
You don't need to worry.

00:11:10.010 --> 00:11:12.030
Pass or fail, I've decided to

00:11:12.030 --> 00:11:13.730
become a baker, no matter what.

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:16.500
All right.

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:24.120
Y-You should get that.

00:11:27.590 --> 00:11:30.080
Hello? This is Wolf.

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:31.700
Yes...

00:11:33.390 --> 00:11:35.270
Oh, I see.

00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:37.500
Yes, I understand.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:38.550
Thank you.

00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:44.010
H-How'd it go?

00:11:56.310 --> 00:11:57.300
I got it!

00:11:57.750 --> 00:11:59.230
I got it, Tiger!

00:12:05.650 --> 00:12:08.060
You did it, you lug!

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:10.920
All right! We're going to 
the Grizzly Bar tonight!

00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:14.110
Great job, Wolf, you rascal!

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:18.920
I see.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:22.070
Drink until you pass out tonight.

00:12:22.070 --> 00:12:23.130
It's on the house!

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:26.570
All right! I'll take a martini.

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:28.100
I'd like a bourbon.

00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:30.230
I'll take a scotch!

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:36.640
Who the hell said it'd be 
on the house for you?!

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:42.950
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:42.010
Mr. Penguin's New Love!

00:12:47.980 --> 00:12:51.470
Mr. Penguin hasn't 
been by much lately.

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:55.330
Now that you mention it...

00:12:55.990 --> 00:12:58.490
I thought it was rather quiet.

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:01.220
I guess it's because 
Mr. Penguin's not here.

00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:03.900
I wonder if he's been busy.

00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:04.940
Who knows?

00:13:04.940 --> 00:13:06.200
Maybe he took a vacation?

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:08.790
I ran into him.

00:13:10.030 --> 00:13:11.410
You did?

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:13.140
Yes, yesterday.

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:15.200
Where at?

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:17.100
The next town.

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:24.290
Huh?

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:25.730
Mr. Penguin?

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:27.450
Mr. Llama?!

00:13:28.010 --> 00:13:30.650
What are you doing here?

00:13:30.650 --> 00:13:33.410
Oh, um... uh...

00:13:33.410 --> 00:13:37.620
Brown Bear's 
Café

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:36.930
Brown Bear's Café?

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:38.700
Yes.

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:42.840
It's a café in the next town 
run by Mr. Brown Bear.

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:45.240
Brown Bear runs Brown Bear's Café?

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:48.670
Not very original, is it?

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:51.810
The same could be said 
about Polar Bear's Café.

00:13:52.950 --> 00:13:55.970
Mr. Penguin was saying he's 
been going every day.

00:13:56.290 --> 00:13:57.670
Every day?

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:02.270
I wonder if Mr. Penguin got 
tired of Polar Bear's Café.

00:14:03.600 --> 00:14:05.740
Well, he was always here.

00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:08.930
He was always here.

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:11.610
Listen to this, Miss Sasako.

00:14:11.610 --> 00:14:15.370
I figured out a non-embarrassing 
way to take home leftovers

00:14:15.820 --> 00:14:19.670
when I can't finish eating.

00:14:20.720 --> 00:14:23.130
He was always talking, wasn't he?

00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:26.590
He was always talking.

00:14:27.250 --> 00:14:28.550
Could I get another café mocha?

00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:32.050
As long as I have a café mocha 
from Polar Bear's Café,

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:33.870
I don't need anything else.

00:14:34.370 --> 00:14:35.810
But I do need fish, though.

00:14:36.570 --> 00:14:38.140
So you do need something.

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:41.610
He was always drinking 
café mocha, wasn't he?

00:14:42.690 --> 00:14:45.070
Maybe he got tired of café mochas?

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:49.960
Maybe Brown Bear's Café's café mocha

00:14:49.960 --> 00:14:52.530
tastes better than Polar 
Bear's Café's?

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:57.230
Mr. Penguin is allowed to be at 
any café he wants to be at.

00:14:57.230 --> 00:14:59.070
That's true, but...

00:14:59.560 --> 00:15:01.510
It's a little lonely, don't you think?

00:15:01.510 --> 00:15:03.290
He was always here.

00:15:03.290 --> 00:15:05.250
He really was always here.

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:09.840
Aren't you the least bit lonely, Mr. Polar Bear?

00:15:26.170 --> 00:15:27.320
Welcome.

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:30.420
Hello.

00:15:36.690 --> 00:15:39.710
Pardon me. Could I get 
a café mocha, please?

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:42.210
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:46.670
Thank you for waiting.

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:52.990
<i>Oh?</i>

00:15:52.990 --> 00:15:56.170
<i>There's a bit too much 
chocolate syrup.</i>

00:15:58.980 --> 00:16:00.400
Welcome.

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:01.900
Hello.

00:16:03.950 --> 00:16:05.610
Please have a seat 
wherever you'd like.

00:16:06.290 --> 00:16:07.740
Th-Thanks.

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:17.700
Polar Bear?

00:16:19.610 --> 00:16:21.020
But I'm a panda.

00:16:21.020 --> 00:16:22.420
Your cover was immediately blown.

00:16:22.880 --> 00:16:24.050
You're long.

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:30.460
Polar Bear,

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:33.450
sorry I haven't been 
by the café lately.

00:16:34.450 --> 00:16:37.930
You're allowed to go to any 
café you want, Mr. Penguin.

00:16:40.460 --> 00:16:43.060
Are you angry, by chance?

00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:45.590
Of course not.

00:16:46.110 --> 00:16:48.300
Okay, good.

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:55.070
Do you like this café's 
café mocha?

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:02.910
They make it too sweet here,
and I don't really like it.

00:17:04.130 --> 00:17:05.370
Then why?

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:06.410
Huh?

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:08.770
Well, uh...

00:17:09.310 --> 00:17:10.410
Welcome.

00:17:15.410 --> 00:17:17.800
Are you ready to order?

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:20.560
W-Well... Um!

00:17:21.130 --> 00:17:22.530
C-Could I get my usual?

00:17:22.940 --> 00:17:25.460
I'm sorry, your usual?

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:28.360
C-Could I get a café mocha?

00:17:28.790 --> 00:17:31.150
Sure. One café mocha.

00:17:31.810 --> 00:17:33.390
It'll be out shortly.

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:43.730
So that's it.

00:17:45.970 --> 00:17:46.710
Yeah.

00:17:48.190 --> 00:17:49.820
That's how it is.

00:17:50.230 --> 00:17:52.160
So, Polar Bear,

00:17:52.160 --> 00:17:54.050
I'm sorry I haven't been to the Café.

00:17:55.790 --> 00:17:56.680
Mr. Penguin.

00:17:58.150 --> 00:17:58.890
What?

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:02.850
We're friends, even if you don't 
come by the Café, right?

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:06.400
Polar Bear...

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:10.270
I'll be rooting for you, Mr. Penguin.

00:18:10.750 --> 00:18:12.950
Thanks, Polar Bear!

00:18:12.950 --> 00:18:15.810
I'll keep stopping by 
Brown Bear's Café

00:18:15.810 --> 00:18:17.610
until I can ask her out!

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:19.610
Okay, got it.

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:21.460
I'm gonna do my best.

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:24.750
I want to hurry and drink 
one of your café mochas.

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:28.140
Tell Panda and the others 
I said "hi," as well.

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:33.600
Oh, I'm beat.

00:18:33.600 --> 00:18:36.890
It's so hard to laze
 around at work.

00:18:38.060 --> 00:18:41.140
I'm going to go laze 
around at home now.

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:44.100
So there's more than 
one kind of lazing around...

00:18:44.840 --> 00:18:48.680
Oh, Mr. Penguin didn't 
come today, either?

00:18:48.680 --> 00:18:51.380
Oh, yes...

00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:53.570
I wonder what's going on.

00:18:55.260 --> 00:18:56.390
Well, you see...

00:18:57.030 --> 00:19:00.490
Brown Bear's 
Café

00:19:02.390 --> 00:19:04.520
H-Hello.

00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:06.090
Hello.

00:19:08.100 --> 00:19:09.920
Oh, would you like your usual?

00:19:12.730 --> 00:19:14.380
Y-Yes, please!

00:19:17.320 --> 00:19:21.210
What? Mr. Penguin has a new crush?

00:19:21.980 --> 00:19:23.350
He said he wouldn't be able

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:25.150
to come here until he asks her out,

00:19:25.150 --> 00:19:26.810
so he asked me to say hi for him.

00:19:27.710 --> 00:19:32.230
It took him quite a while to ask 
out Miss Penko, didn't it?

00:19:32.750 --> 00:19:35.830
He might not be able to 
come by for a couple years.

00:20:00.610 --> 00:20:02.550
P-Pardon me.

00:20:04.610 --> 00:20:05.510
Yes?

00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:12.510
Um...

00:20:23.260 --> 00:20:25.820
Wow, the Bears won.

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:29.310
I see.

00:20:30.050 --> 00:20:31.320
Mr. Penguin.

00:20:31.810 --> 00:20:34.300
You're not going to Brown 
Bear's Café today?

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:38.420
My only café is Polar 
Bear's Café after all.

00:20:39.370 --> 00:20:42.840
Meaning you got rejec—

00:20:44.290 --> 00:20:45.680
Panda.

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:48.430
Please leave him be 
at times like these.

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:50.390
It's okay, Miss Sasako.

00:21:01.010 --> 00:21:05.500
The café mochas here are always 
so good that I can't stop myself.

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:08.620
Hey, Miss Sasako, Panda.

00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:10.120
Yes?

00:21:11.010 --> 00:21:13.760
Could you two cheer me up right now?

00:21:14.260 --> 00:21:17.540
Tell me <i>all</i> the great things about me!

00:21:18.520 --> 00:21:20.080
Right now?

00:21:20.080 --> 00:21:22.510
Yeah! Just now! Right now!

00:21:23.160 --> 00:21:25.170
Come on now, let's hurry it up.

00:21:25.170 --> 00:21:27.290
Come on!

00:21:27.290 --> 00:21:28.970
This is so sudden...

00:21:29.640 --> 00:21:33.300
Polar Bear's Café just isn't the same

00:21:33.300 --> 00:21:35.530
without Mr. Penguin being a nuisance.

00:21:36.930 --> 00:21:38.980
Right, Polar Bear?

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:39.940
Right.

00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:41.550
What the heck?

00:21:42.170 --> 00:21:47.100
I feel like I'm being praised 
and attacked at the same time.

00:21:48.050 --> 00:21:49.990
Would you like another café mocha?

00:21:51.870 --> 00:21:53.160
Yeah, I think I would.

00:21:54.810 --> 00:21:59.060
All right. Bring on the praises!

00:21:59.060 --> 00:22:01.040
Sorry, we're sold out.

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:04.380
Then, Miss Sasako...

00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:06.870
Huh? Well, let's see...

00:22:06.870 --> 00:22:07.890
I'm out of stock.

00:22:07.890 --> 00:22:09.810
You, too, Miss Sasako?!

00:22:09.810 --> 00:22:12.910
I think all of the good things 
about you were so popular,

00:22:12.910 --> 00:22:14.570
that they all got bought up.

00:22:14.570 --> 00:22:17.410
Quit being witty and say something

00:22:17.410 --> 00:22:19.830
good about me, Polar Bear!

00:23:54.990 --> 00:24:24.990
Next Time

00:23:58.040 --> 00:23:59.660
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.660 --> 00:24:00.830
What is it, Panda?

00:24:00.830 --> 00:24:03.160
If you know of some discovery 
worthy of the Nobel Prize,

00:24:03.160 --> 00:24:04.350
you should let me know.

00:24:04.350 --> 00:24:05.500
I don't think I know of any.

00:24:05.500 --> 00:24:06.830
Even if I did, I wouldn't tell you

00:24:06.830 --> 00:24:08.340
and I'd get the Nobel Prize myself.

00:24:08.340 --> 00:24:10.840
Then how about a normal discovery?

00:24:10.840 --> 00:24:12.250
When you're late,

00:24:12.250 --> 00:24:15.610
saying you were in a hurry 
usually gets you out of trouble.

00:24:15.610 --> 00:24:17.320
That's a rather small discovery.

00:24:17.320 --> 00:24:18.600
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:18.600 --> 00:24:20.170
Next week's Polar Bear's Café

00:24:20.170 --> 00:24:21.490
will only have one moving part.

00:24:21.490 --> 00:24:22.560
Let's make sure it's 
moving in general.

00:24:21.620 --> 00:24:24.550
Sloth Wants To Work
Mr. Handa's Present

00:24:22.560 --> 00:24:23.950
Enjoy!
